new:
{
  "id": "grammar.c1.32.03.adv-human-dignity-absoluteness",
  "title": "Recap: Stance Adverbials and Reasons",
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "How it works",
      "content": "You know stance adverbials from C1 Unit 12 (*lelkiismereti okból*, *meggyőződéstől vezérelve*). The same frames fit the language of dignity: `erkölcsi okból` (for moral reasons), `a méltóság tiszteletétől vezérelve` (guided by respect for dignity). New in this lesson is the vocabulary of dignity. Sólyom László called human dignity an *anyajog*, a right from which other rights can come; this is his term, and jurists have debated it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Example",
      "content": "Example: `Erkölcsi okból is fontos az emberi méltóság védelme.`"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Patterns in Context",
      "rows": [
        [
          "Erkölcsi okból is fontos az emberi méltóság védelme.",
          "For moral reasons too the protection of human dignity is important."
        ],
        [
          "A méltóság tiszteletétől vezérelve döntött így a bíró.",
          "Guided by respect for dignity, the judge decided so."
        ],
        [
          "Az elidegeníthetetlen jogról az ember nem mondhat le.",
          "A person cannot give up an inalienable right."
        ]
      ]
    }
  ]
}

